      "entity_type": "solution",
      "path": ".cg-docs/solutions/data-quality/2026-04-12-country-code-case-sensitivity-silent-empty-filter.md",
      "slug": "2026-04-12-country-code-case-sensitivity-silent-empty-filter",
      "status": "",
      "summary": "A user calls a data-access function with lowercase or mixed-case country codes: The function returns an empty `data.table` with 0 rows and no error or warning. The lookup logic uses `dt[[\"iso3c\"]] %in% country`, and the stored codes are all uppercase (`\"NOR\"`, `\"SWE\"`), so `%in%` finds no match. This is a common user mistake — ISO3C codes are conventionally uppercase but that convention is not enforced at entry points.",
