      "status": "",
      "summary": "When reshaping a `data.table` from wide to long with `melt()`, the `variable` column (controlled by `variable.name`) is returned as a **factor** by default: This pattern appeared **four times** in the same vignette. Each occurrence: 1. Allocates an intermediate factor object. 2. Calls `as.character()` to create a second allocation. 3. Uses the character result as a lookup key into a named vector.",
